uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, yes, yes. Okay.\par \par \uc2 INSOOK KIM GAYLE (MOTHER OF EVA PILGRIM)\par \par \uc2 This is a Mother's Day present.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, you got it. So, we know their product, Poo-pourri. This is the bathroom spray that everybody knows, but they also now have these great products that for any room in your house. And this is an odor eliminator. It will eliminate 99% of odors, even cigarette odor in an instant. So, whether you use it on fabric, carpet, in the air, it doesn't just mask it, it eliminates it. So, for any kind of odor situation, they've got a product for you. We put together a bunch of bundles. They start at $17.50 and?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: POURRI, 50% OFF\par \par \uc2 INSOOK KIM GAYLE (MOTHER OF EVA PILGRIM)\par \par \uc2 Free shipping.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You got it. Okay. \uc2 Butter London\uc2 . So, \uc2 Butter London\uc2  makes really beautiful nail polishes, lipsticks. We've got a couple of collections from them. A couple of their new products as well. One of their new lip products or makeup products, I should say, is their Lumi matte collection. It's kind of a no makeup-makeup look, so that you can look flawless but natural.\par \par \uc2 INSOOK KIM GAYLE (MOTHER OF EVA PILGRIM)\par \par \uc2 Natural.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, exactly. Plus, we've got all of their bright new colors for lips. We even have, I mean for nails. I'm mixing up lips and tips, but we also have their nail treatments. One of their most popular is mellow the yellow, which is a really phenomenal thing. All of these products today start at $6 and?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BUTTER LONDON, 50% - 70% OFF\par \par \uc2 INSOOK KIM GAYLE (MOTHER OF EVA PILGRIM)\par \par \uc2 Free shipping.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You got it. And finally, we're ending on a note of comfort. Blanquil, this is a weighted blanket. So, inside here...\par \par \uc2 INSOOK KIM GAYLE (MOTHER OF EVA PILGRIM)\par \par \uc2 I love it.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...a 15-pound and 20-pound. You choose it based on your weight and the duvet cover comes off for easy washing. This is like a gentle hug, helps you relax, destress to go to sleep. These are 50% off, $84.50, comes in three colors and, of course, with every one?\par \par \uc2 INSOOK KIM GAYLE (MOTHER OF EVA PILGRIM)\par \par \uc2 Free shipping.\par \par \uc2 TORY JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You got it. She's hired. Let's bring her back next week.\par \par \uc2 EVA PILGRIM (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Thanks, Tory. And all these deals are on our website and we partnered with these companies. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220523ei570003n\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 THOMAS: INSTITUTION CAN'T BE 'BULLIED' URGENT INVESTIGATION INTO SUPREME COURT DRAFT LEAK\b0\par\par\uc2 905 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 May 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Saturday\par \uc2 WNSA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 UKRAINE, RUSSIA, INVASION, BIDEN, BURNS, ZELENSKYY\par \par \uc2 WILDFIRE, EVACUATION, BURNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CRITICAL FIRE DANGER\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, TRACK, FLOODING, WIND, HEAT\par \par \uc2 BAHAMAS, DARVILLE, PROBE, CHIARELLI, SANDALS RESORTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AMERICAN TOURISTS' DEATH INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 HEPATITIS, CHILDREN, BHATT, ADENOVIRUS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING HEPATITIS OUTBREAK\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, ROE V. WADE, PROTEST, THOMAS, GIRGIS, HARRIS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THOMAS: INSTITUTION CAN'T BE 'BULLIED'\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, as the abortion debate intensifies, Supreme Court Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  is speaking out. According to Reuters, the conservative telling a judicial conference, "The institution can't be bullied." And now, the investigation underway into who leaked that explosive draft opinion on Roe v. Wade. ABC's White House correspondent Karen Travers, at the Supreme Court, tonight.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: URGENT INVESTIGATION INTO SUPREME COURT DRAFT LEAK\par \par \uc2 KAREN TRAVER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Following that leaked draft opinion that shows the Supreme Court appears ready to overturn Roe v. Wade, conservative Justice \uc2 Clarence Thomas\uc2  speaking out, insisting at a judicial conference Friday, according to Reuters, that the court, quote, "can't be an institution that can be bullied into giving you just the outcomes you want." Abortion front and center, again, today. Protesters taking a stand at the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 KAREN TRAVER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was your reaction when that draft opinion came out the other day, when it was leaked?\par \par \uc2 PROTESTER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Total disgust. Total disgust, and just sadness. I have a daughter. I want her to be able to have human rights, just like my son has.\par \par \uc2 KAREN TRAVER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The White House not staying quiet, either. Vice President Harris today revving up \uc2 Tennessee State University\uc2  graduates.\par \par \uc2 VICE PRESIDENT KAMALA HARRIS (UNITED STATES)\par \par \uc2 The world that you graduate into is unsettled. It is a world where long-established principles now rest on shaky ground, principles like the freedom to vote, the rights of women to make decisions about their own bodies.\par \par \uc2 KAREN TRAVER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Back here in Washington, the mystery still swirling, who leaked that draft opinion that could upend the nearly 50-year-old landmark decision that gave women constitutional cover for the right to an abortion? An internal investigation led by Marshal of the Court Gail Curley, a career Army lawyer, has already begun. A key focus? The paper trail. Justices do, after all, circulate copies of draft opinions for feedback. Those drafts strictly confidential.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ACCESS TO LEAKED DRAFT OPINION\par \par \uc2 KAREN TRAVER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Only the nine justices, roughly 30 administrative staff, and 37 clerks, the young lawyers who do much of the research and writing, have access.\par \par \uc2 SHERIF GIRGIS (FORMER SUPREME COURT CLERK TO JUSTICE SAMUEL ALITO)\par \par \uc2 I find it very hard to imagine a healthy, functioning court next year if the person who made the leak isn't identified, publicly identified, and sanctioned for it.\par \par \uc2 KAREN TRAVER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The nation, meanwhile, holding its breath to see if the court overturns Roe, leaving any regulations up to individual states.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CERTAIN OR LIKELY TO BAN ABORTION\par \par \uc2 KAREN TRAVER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Twenty-six states are certain or likely to outlaw abortion entirely, if Roe falls.\par \par \uc2 KAREN TRAVER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Whit, some of the abortion rights activists I spoke to today here say they want to see Congress take action to protect the right to an abortion. Senate Democrats, this week, will try to move forward on legislation to do that, but it is almost certain to fail because of Republican opposition. Whit?\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Karen Travers, in Washington. Our thanks to you, tonight. And for more on the Supreme Court leak, tune into "This Week" tomorrow morning.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEN. AMY KLOBUCHAR (D) MINNESOTA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOV. ASA HUTCHINSON (R) ARKANSAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THIS WEEK SUNDAY\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Martha Raddatz has exclusive interviews with Senator Amy Klobuchar and Arkansas Governor Asa Hutchison about the future of abortion rights in America.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUBWAY ATTACK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUSPECT FACES TERROR CHARGES\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Tonight, the man accused of shooting 10 people on a New York subway is facing terror charges that could land him in prison for life.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) A federal grand jury in Brooklyn has returned a two-count indictment against Frank James for allegedly discharging a firearm and carrying out a terror attack on a transit system. No one was killed in the April 12th attack, which authorities have said James planned well in advance.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TALIBAN IN AFGHANISTAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN ORDERED TO WEAR BURQAS\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Now to Afghanistan, and some of the fears of human rights activists are being realized.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The \uc2 Taliban\uc2  once again requiring women to cover up head to toe in public, ordering them to show only their eyes and recommending the use of the full-body burqas. Hard-line leaders restoring similar restrictions from when they last held power 20 years ago. The decree also encourages women to stay at home, unless they have important work.\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And there is much more ahead on "World News Tonight" this Saturday.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WORLD NEWS TONIGHT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMING UP\par \par \uc2 WHIT JOHNSON (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Suspected deadly overdoses strike \uc2 Ohio State University\uc2  following the school's dire drug warning to students. And the death toll climbs and search efforts intensify after that horrific explosion at a Havana hotel.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 Document WNSA000020220510ei5700007\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 SUPREME COURT SCRAMBLE DEMOCRATS RACE TO PROTECT ACCESS TO ABORTION\b0\par\par\uc2 592 \uc2 words\par \uc2 6 May 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: VACCINE BOMBSHELL\par \par \uc2 COVID, FDA, J&J, BLOOD CLOTS, BROWNSTEIN, BURKEY\par \par \uc2 JHA, FDA, COVID, VACCINE, J&J, PAXLOVID, FUNDING\par \par \uc2 WALL STREET, STOCKS, INFLATION, DOW, RESERVE\par \par \uc2 COURT, SCHUMER, ABORTION, COLLINS, PSAKI, LAMONT\par \par \uc2 CECILIA VEGA (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, Rebecca, thank you so much. We're going to turn now to the latest on the battle over abortion after that draft Supreme Court opinion leak. Democrats scrambling in the event the court overturns Roe V. Wade, Rachel Scott is tracking it all this morning. And, Rachel, Democrats and the White House realizing they've got very few options on this one.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT SCRAMBLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEMOCRATS RACE TO PROTECT ACCESS TO ABORTION IN WAKE OF LEAKED DRAFT DECISION\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Cecilia, good morning. Extremely limited options. Democrats have been desperately trying to find a path forward to protect access to abortion for millions of women in this country. They do have a plan, but they do not have the Republican support they need to get it done.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) This morning with the Supreme Court possibly poised to overturn Roe versus Wade, Democrats are scrambling to find ways to protect access to abortion.\par \par \uc2 JEN PSAKI\uc2  (WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY)\par \par \uc2 We are looking at a broad range of options.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The Biden administration promising a fight, but not offering very many specifics. Over on Capitol Hill, Senate Democrats are pushing forward with a vote on legislation that would secure abortion access for millions.\par \par \uc2 SEN CHARLES SCHUMER (DEM) (NEW YORK/MAJORITY LEADER)\par \par \uc2 Next week's vote will be one of the most important we take, not only this session, but in this century. Republicans will not be able to hide from the horror they've unleashed on America.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But that bill is almost certain to fail. Democrats don't have enough Republican support to get it passed. Only two Republican Senators support abortion rights, \uc2 Susan Collins\uc2  and Lisa Murkowski. Both support legislation that would make a woman's right to obtain an abortion a federal law.\par \par \uc2 SEN SUSAN COLLINS (REP) (MAINE)\par \par \uc2 My goal is to codify what is essentially existing law. That means Roe V. Wade.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) But Collins declared she will not support the Democrats' bill because it goes too far. This as states race to put their own rules in place before the Supreme Court ruling. Republican lawmakers in Louisiana advanced a bill to classify abortion as a homicide, as Connecticut's Democratic Governor signed a bill protecting patients traveling there from states that have outlawed abortion.\par \par \uc2 GOV NED LAMONT (DEM) (CONNECTICUT)\par \par \uc2 No politician is going to get between you and your doctor.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING FALLOUT FROM SUPREME COURT LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORT: CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS CALLS BREACH "ABSOLUTELY APPALLING"\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Outside the Supreme Court, demonstrators face off, as investigations into who leaked that opinion draft continues. Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  reportedly telling a judicial conference the leak was "Absolutely appalling." Roberts saying he hoped "One bad apple" wouldn't change the way Americans view the Supreme Court.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And that is the question hanging over all of this. What are the political consequences of that leak. Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  reportedly said that it will not affect the decision-making process, but what upsets him is that it gives the wrong impression to people dedicated to serving the high court. George.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220523ei5600005\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TERRA JOLE'S HEALTH BATTLE "LITTLE WOMEN: LA" STAR OPENS UP ABOUT CANCER\b0\par\par\uc2 870 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 May 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 STORM, TORNADOES, FOSTER, POWER OUTAGE\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, TRACK, STORM, TORNADOES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORM THREAT ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHERE THE DANGEROUS WEATHER IS HEADING NEXT\par \par \uc2 DRAFT, LEAK, ABORTION, BIDEN\par \par \uc2 RUSSIA, INVASION, UKRAINE\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, CASES, PROJECTIONS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW COVID CONCERNS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: HOSPITAL ADMISSIONS & DEATHS PROJECTED TO RISE IN COMING WEEKS\par \par \uc2 CHAPPELLE, INVESTIGATION, LEE, FOXX, ROCK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DAVE CHAPPELLE ATTACK INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS ABOUT SUSPECT IN VIOLENT ASSAULT\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, KEELY, INVESTIGATION, WHITE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JAILBREAK MANHUNT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW DETAILS ABOUT "SPECIAL RELATIONSHIP" BETWEEN MURDER SUSPECT & OFFICER\par \par \uc2 PARTON, ROCK & ROLL HALL OF FAME, INDUCTEES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DOLLY INDUCTED INTO ROCK & ROLL HALL OF FAME\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PARTON "HONORED AND HUMBLED\u8230\'20\'26WILL ACCEPTS IT GRACEFULLY"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 DEFAMATION, TRIAL, HEARD, DEPP\par \par \uc2 CARS, THEFT, VOSS, CATALYTIC CONVERTERS\par \par \uc2 BOX OFFICE, MOVIES, CRUISE, TELLER, "TOP GUN"\par \par \uc2 SULLIVAN, SKYDIVING, BIRTHDAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: AHEAD ON GMA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TURBOTAX SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORM THREAT ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 TORNADO, WEATHER, OKLAHOMA, TEXAS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE STORMS CAUSE WIDESPREAD DEVASTATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: REPORTED TORNADOES TOUCH DOWN IN OK & TX\par \par \uc2 WEATHER, STORM, FORECAST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STORM THREAT ON THE MOVE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHERE THE DANGEROUS WEATHER IS HEADING NEXT\par \par \uc2 TURBOTAX, TAXES, SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR TURBOTAX SETTLEMENT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: COMPANY TO PAY $141 MILLION OVER CLAIMS\par \par \uc2 JOLE, "LITTLE WOMEN: LA", BREAST CANCER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TERRA JOLE'S HEALTH BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "LITTLE WOMEN: LA" STAR OPENS UP ABOUT CANCER\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are looking forward to that, but right now we have our "GMA" cover story. "Little Women: LA" star and "Dancing with the Stars" alum Terra Jole is speaking about her breast cancer diagnosis and what's next in her health journey. Kaylee Hartung sat down with her, and she's back with her story. Good morning again, Kaylee.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Good morning, again, Robin. Terra Jole's first red flag came when breast-feeding. She knew something didn't feel right. Now, nearly a year later, she is fighting, determined to take control of her future.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She's a warrior on the dance floor and a shining star on "Little Women: LA."\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM "LITTLE WOMEN: LA"\par \par \uc2 TERRA JOLE ("LITTLE WOMEN: LA")\par \par \uc2 It just shows me that my relationship with her has just gone down the tubes.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now, 4'2" Terra Jole sharing a personal health battle with her fans after finding a lump in her breast.\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM "LITTLE WOMEN: LA"\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Writing on \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , "I have breast cancer. Hardest call I've ever made was this video telling my mom for the first time."\par \par \uc2 TV CLIP FROM "LITTLE WOMEN: LA"\par \par \uc2 TERRA JOLE ("LITTLE WOMEN: LA")\par \par \uc2 Next week I am having a double mastectomy because I have breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 MOTHER OF TERRA JOLE (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 A double mastectomy, oh, TJ, oh my goodness.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ON HER DOUBLE MASTECTOMY & THE NEXT STEPS IN HER JOURNEY\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) We sat down with the mom of three just eight days after her surgery. She says she opted for a double mastectomy hoping to avoid a recurrence of the cancer.\par \par \uc2 TERRA JOLE ("LITTLE WOMEN: LA")\par \par \uc2 I didn't want that for my children. I didn't want to go through this multiple times, and so I want to take both now and not have to think about what if in the future.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Jole also dealing with a condition called skeletal dysplasia that causes her short stature.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Your whole life you've fought to make your disability an ability. How does that mentality carry through now?\par \par \uc2 TERRA JOLE ("LITTLE WOMEN: LA")\par \par \uc2 Showing that you're not alone through an experience like this, whether you're little, whether you're average, this can happen to anyone.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Now Jole is looking ahead.\par \par \uc2 TERRA JOLE ("LITTLE WOMEN: LA")\par \par \uc2 We're doing everything to catch everything. So, I'm going to be able to see my kids when they walk down the aisle or have children of their own. It's been my main focus is, like, how do I get back to being a mom fulltime?\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 She calls her husband Joe her backbone, but he says Jole is his family's rock.\par \par \uc2 JOE GNOFFO (TERRA HUSBAND)\par \par \uc2 I can't believe how she's handling this. Never once have I heard, like, why me, or she's just not like that.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And Jole has a message for all women.\par \par \uc2 TERRA JOLE ("LITTLE WOMEN: LA")\par \par \uc2 If you feel something, say something. And it can be a matter of life or death for you.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So, if you do feel something abnormal, make sure to talk to a doctor about the next right steps for you. Double mastectomies are not appropriate for all women with breast cancer, but Terra and her doctors felt like it was the right move for her. Guys.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We hope she's doing well.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We do.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Thank you, Kaylee.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020220520ei550003d\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 CELEBRATING OUR MOTHERS MEET LARA'S MOM CAROLYN\b0\par\par\uc2 2,072 \uc2 words\par \uc2 4 May 2022\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2022, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPREME COURT LEAK FALLOUT\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, LEAK, "POLITICO", ABORTION, HARRIS, WARREN\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, DRAFT, BIDEN, ROE V. WADE\par \par \uc2 JUSTICES, LEAK, ABORTION, FALLOUT, STATES\par \par \uc2 WAR, UKRAINE, EVACUATE, SHELTERS, ATTACKS\par \par \uc2 GRINER, RUSSIA, CUSTODY, STATE DEPT, WNBA\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, STOCKS, FEDERAL RESERVE, INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 MORANT, GRIZZLIES, WARRIORS, NBA PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW SEVERE WEATHER THREAT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM "STAR WARS"\par \par \uc2 CHAPPELLE, ATTACK, ARREST, ROCK, FOXX, BOWL\par \par \uc2 MANHUNT, JAILBREAK, WHITE, SINGLETON, VIDEO\par \par \uc2 SINGLETON, WHITE, SUSPECT, MANHUNT, ROMANCE\par \par \uc2 JUDGE, HOMERUN, \uc2 BLUE JAYS\uc2 , \uc2 YANKEES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SEVERE WEATHER MOVES EAST\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING FALLOUT\par \par \uc2 SUPREME COURT, LEAK, ABORTION, PROTEST\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GROWING FALLOUT FROM SUPREME COURT LEAK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW PROTESTS AS CHIEF JUSTICE ORDERS INVESTIGATION\par \par \uc2 FLIGHT, ASSAULT, SENTENCING, COURT\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIDAIR MELTDOWN SENTENCING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAN TAPED TO SEAT ASSAULT GIVEN 60 DAYS\par \par \uc2 INFLATION, FEDERAL RESERVE, INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BATTLING INFLATION\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL RESERVE EXPECTED TO HIKE INTEREST RATES\par \par \uc2 ABORTION, TRAVEL, STATES, LAW\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FACES OF THE ABORTION BATTLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WOMEN WHO TRAVELED FOR PROCEDURE SHARE STORIES\par \par \uc2 BIEBER, MENTAL HEALTH, MARRIAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JUSTIN BIEBER GETS CANDID\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SUPERSTAR TALKS MARRIAGE & MENTAL HEALTH\par \par \uc2 RYAN, SWIFT, HALL OF FAME, PUPPY\par \par \uc2 HART, BOOK, "MARCUS MAKES IT BIG"\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: KEVIN HART ONE-ON-ONE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: STAR TALKS NEW KIDS' BOOK "MARCUS MAKES IT BIG"\par \par \uc2 "THE CHANGE", MILLER, BOOK CLUB\par \par \uc2 STORY2\par \par \uc2 CUMBERBATCH, ACTOR, "DOCTOR STRANGE", MARVEL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BENEDICT CUMBERBATCH LIVE IN TIMES SQUARE\par \par \uc2 LUJAN, STROKE, AWARENESS, HEALTH\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATOR BEN RAY LUJAN OPENS UP ABOUT HIS STROKE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RAISING AWARENESS AFTER EXPERIENCING ONE AT AGE 49\par \par \uc2 "OBI-WAN KENOBI", MCGREGOR\par \par \uc2 MOTHERS, COOKING, SPENCER, COWBOY CASSEROLE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CELEBRATING OUR MOTHERS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MEET LARA'S MOM CAROLYN\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We are back now with our Momma's Favorite Dish series as we count down to Mother's Day, and this morning, you brought your sweet mother.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I did, I did. She's so cute. She's hiding over there, ready for her big, grand entrance. She is the woman would taught me how to navigate flea markets and tag sales like no other. The youngest of five kids, I got to tag along with mom quite a lot, and as a result, we've always been best friends. Here's a look at how special she is.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) My relationship with my mom is incredible. She's my best friend, my adviser.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 She was the baby in the family, and she just brought a great deal of pleasure to us from that day until right now.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And one of our most special memory, our family dinners. Like, dinner was no joke. We all finished our plate.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Or no dessert.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Or no dessert, which was, like, a fate worse than you know what.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And mom's specialty, her famous cowboy casserole.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Cowboy casserole was a great example of my mom trying to get it done for a family of seven. In one dish, it had your meat, your vegetable, some starch because it had biscuits on top. It's a legendary dish in our house.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 This is true.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) For better or worse, you're getting cowboy casserole.\par \par \uc2 SENATOR BEN RAY LUJAN (DEM) (NEW MEXICO)\par \par \uc2 Let's do it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, those photos, priceless.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, there are some good looks in there, but she is priceless.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let us bring out, with no further ado, Miss Carolyn. Come on out.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) There she is.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Wonderful to see you again. Thank you, thank you, thank you, thank you. So, before we get cooking, the youngest of five. Come on, give us some dirt. What was this kid like? What was this child...?\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Busy, very busy. Youngest of five. She, you know, had to make her own way in the family, and she certainly did.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) She was just trying to keep up.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Look at, look at mom's hair. Did you, you missed it.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, I love, I love these throwback photos that we're seeing there.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, I don't love that one, but...\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Where are you looking?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I don't know. That was my come hither look.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Let's get to it. I know you love all your children equally. That's what mothers always say like that.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Oh, absolutely.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Robin's also the youngest of five, by the way.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Youngest of four, yeah, yeah, four.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, that's right. I knew we were both youngest.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, so let's get cooking here. So, we have these ingredients here. First of all, tell folks again what we're making.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Cowboy casserole and, mom, this is a great example of you just trying to get it done.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely. When you have to feed a family of seven, and they're all very busy, involved in sports and whatever, you try and make something that's relatively easy, you can do it in advance and hearty.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, and casseroles are always a big hit with families. So, tell us the ingredients that you have here.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Most of the time.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Most of the time, yes.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This version, I don't use the meat because I'm more of a plant-based diet. My mom used to use, what kind of meat did you use?\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 I used to use a stewing beef.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Or ground beef is how many recipes call for it. I think it was like whatever we had leftover. So, onions and garlic.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 No, it wasn't.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I, but I digress. So onions and garlic, right, with a little bit of oil. Once those get translucent, you can add your spices. Robin, jump in there.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, sure.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You've got cumin, you've got chili pepper, you've got salt and pepper. And the heat will really release the flavors of those. So that saut\u233\'00\'E9s for a little bit. Again, when the onions get translucent, you your add veggies and your beans. You've got garbanzo beans, you've got black beans.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, I love garbanzos.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You can use any kind of bean that you want. I know you used to use kidney beans, my worst nightmare, so we've exchanged those to, canned tomato sauce.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All of this?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yeah, canned corn, really easy, right? I mean, all of this. Are we, how are we doing?\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 So far so good.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) What was it like cooking together growing up? Did she help?\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Well, actually I used to banish Lara from the kitchen.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You did?\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Yeah, she was on cleanup duty.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Was she? Oh. Well, that's a real story.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) I was on cleanup duty. Sort of the same here.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) All right, I'll save you, my friend. So, after we get this, what about the cheese?\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Then, then we add the cheese.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) This boil, has to boil so, to really get all the flavors. Then you add a cup of shredded cheddar and sour cream. I mean, it's really, like, it's, like, really, honestly a great chili. And again, this is a vegetarian version. You can do this keto. You can do this however you want. Cowboy casserole, I looked it up, actually. Mom, you never knew why it was called. It's from the chuckwagon. It was because it was, you know, in the old wild, wild West, which is kind of what it was like at our house.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Very true.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So this all, this goes into a casserole dish, which we would, we would scoop in there. I'm going to save us the time.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Because this is what it is.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) This is what it is. It bakes for how long, Mom?\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 About a half an hour.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, is that all, really?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) About a half an hour. Now, my mom used to bake it with the biscuits raw and put them on raw. So we're so...\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 That's what the recipe said.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) That's what the recipe said. This is not your fault. But what we have discovered was, and we're still suffering with a little PTSD from it, is that the bottoms never cook. So in our modern version, as we've grown, what have we decided?\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 We bake the biscuits first and then put them on.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Oh, that's a great idea.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Push them down.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 And then...\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So they can sop up, you bake this again for another 10 minutes so the biscuits are crispy, but they still sop up the juices.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, and then you put, put some melted cheese...?\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 And then we sprinkle some cheese.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) And the result, my friend, is cowboy casserole. This is Lara's version, which is vegetarian.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) He's coming in, coming in. Michael's coming in.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, get in here, Michael Strahan.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You going to eat that?\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) This is for you.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Okay, thank you.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Come on.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Remember you always used to request it for your birthday.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Yes, I sure did, Mom.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) You can scan the QR code...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Come on, get on there.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) ...on your screen, or you can go to goodmorningamerica.com to get this recipe. Tomorrow, Amy and her mom are going be here to show us one of their family favorites.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 Thank you, Michael. You should have been one of my children.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) I wouldn't have gotten banished from the kitchen.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) Miss Carolyn, thank you, thank you, thank you for bringing this wonderful woman into our lives. We appreciate that.\par \par \uc2 LARA SPENCER (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We love you, momma. Happy Mother's day.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We love you, momma.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (OC) We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 COMMERCIAL BREAK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Momma, Michael really likes this stuff.\par \par \uc2 CAROLYN VON SEELEN (LARA'S MOTHER)\par \par \uc2 I can hear the clicking o